# Scoped vendor-image suppressions for the official mysql:8.4.11 image.
#
# These CRITICAL/HIGH findings are NOT actionable from this application and
# cannot be fixed from this project: they live in the official vendor image
# (FROM mysql:8.4.11) and have no fix in any newer mysql:8.4.x patch image.
# Rebuilding the vendor image is out of scope for this portfolio project.
#
# 1) gosu 1.19 -- prebuilt Go binary (Go stdlib 1.24.6 + golang.org/x/sys 0.1.0)
#    The official image ships a PREBUILT gosu compiled upstream with Go 1.24.6.
#    Trivy's gobinary scanner flags every Go stdlib CVE still open for Go 1.24.6
#    (fixed only in Go 1.24.13 .. 1.25.13 / 1.26.6) plus the pinned
#    golang.org/x/sys advisory GO-2026-5024 / CVE-2026-39824 (fixed in x/sys
#    0.44.0). gosu is required by docker-entrypoint.sh for privilege drop and
#    cannot be patched without MySQL upstream rebuilding it on a newer Go
#    toolchain.
#
# 2) MySQL Shell bundled Python packages (urllib3, cryptography, pyOpenSSL)
#    Installed by the vendor into MySQL Shell's Python environment. They are
#    NOT this application's dependencies; upgrading them in-place risks
#    breaking mysqlsh and no fixed versions are shipped via the MySQL yum repo.
#
# Policy: the Trivy gate stays enabled (severity CRITICAL,HIGH,
# ignore-unfixed true, exit-code 1) for everything NOT listed here.
# Each stdlib advisory is listed in BOTH the CVE and the Go-vulndb (GO-202x-xxxx)
# forms because Trivy may emit either ID for the same gobinary finding.

